The paper confirms the native object is the genus-2 curve \(C_k:Y^2=X^6+k\), with rational points represented exactly as primitive integers \(X=x/y,\;Y=z/y^3\). It also rules out a Track A claim for the simple “small \(k\)” regime: Sections 2–4 give rank, congruence, and elliptic-Chabauty procedures there. The promising route is instead an inverse-generated, high-height rational point family; I’m now checking whether it can honestly support Track B (or must be rejected for lacking a compact solver-visible route).
